 cimei be lo broda would be a set of things that realized 'cimei be lo brod=
a', that is, for every thing among lo cimei lo broda ther are two other thi=
ngs among lo cimei lo broda and thus all three are among lo broda.  So lo c=
imei be lo broda must have at least three members but might have any number=
 at all greater than that.  Now it would seem that lo ci lo broda, since it=
 has an internal quantifier does have exactly three members of lo broda, so=
 it is not the same.
So ultimately the secret of getting groups of the right size in is to get a=
way from 'lo' altogether and quantify directly on the predicates, where we =
get satisfaction, not mere realization,  Or, equivalently, by definition, w=
ork with 'loi' or 'lo'i' depending on how tight a structure you want.



